  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The analysis relies on macro-level historical reconstructions of the U.S. vehicle fleet rather than direct, real-time tracking of individual vehicle usage.",
      "what": "This study reconstructs the long-term growth dynamics of U.S. road vehicles, distinguishing between professional and consumer assets. It introduces a 'usage factor' metric to analyze the divergent patterns of installed power, mass, and fuel energy use across vehicle categories, quantifying decoupling mechanisms like engine oversizing and fleet redundancy.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that avoiding oversized vehicle engines during the transition to electric vehicles can significantly reduce overall material demand, providing a new quantitative link between material immobilization and energy consumption for transport policy."
